## Option C: Use Existing Framework

If you want to skip the plumbing:

### LangChain + Local Model
```python
from langchain_community.llms import Ollama
from langchain.agents import initialize_agent, Tool
import subprocess

llm = Ollama(model="qwen2.5-coder:7b")

tools = [
    Tool(
        name="run_tests",
        func=lambda: subprocess.run(["python3", "secret_spec/test_runner/run_tests.py", 
                                     "--program", "python3 solution.py", "--suite", "public"],
                                   capture_output=True, text=True).stdout,
        description="Run public tests to check progress"
    ),
    Tool(
        name="create_file",
        func=lambda path, code: open(path, "w").write(code),
        description="Create or edit a file with code"
    ),
]

agent = initialize_agent(tools, llm, agent="zero-shot-react-description", verbose=True)
agent.run("Read the spec and implement a solution")
```

### Simpler: Just Use Requests + JSON
```python
import requests
import json

def agent_call(prompt, action_format="json"):
    """Call model and parse structured response"""
    response = requests.post(
        "http://localhost:11434/api/generate",
        json={
            "model": "qwen2.5-coder:7b",
            "prompt": f"{prompt}\n\nRespond in JSON format with 'action', 'details', 'reasoning'",
            "stream": False,
            "format": "json" if action_format == "json" else None
        }
    )
    return json.loads(response.json()["response"])
```

