## Option B: Shell Script + Curl (Ultra-Lightweight)

If you want something even simpler:

```bash
#!/bin/bash

MODEL="qwen2.5-coder:7b"
SPEC="secret_spec/SECRET_SPEC.md"
LOG_DIR="agent_logs"
ITERATION=0
MAX_ITER=20

mkdir -p "$LOG_DIR"

while [ $ITERATION -lt $MAX_ITER ]; do
    echo "=== ITERATION $ITERATION ===" | tee -a "$LOG_DIR/decisions.log"
    
    # Read spec
    SPEC_CONTENT=$(cat "$SPEC")
    
    # Call model with curl
    PROMPT="You are building a solution to this spec:
$SPEC_CONTENT

What is the next step? Choose: EDIT_FILE, RUN_TESTS, or COMPLETE"
    
    RESPONSE=$(curl -s http://localhost:11434/api/generate \
        -d "{\"model\": \"$MODEL\", \"prompt\": \"$PROMPT\", \"stream\": false}" \
        | jq -r '.response')
    
    echo "$RESPONSE" | tee -a "$LOG_DIR/decisions.log"
    
    if echo "$RESPONSE" | grep -q "COMPLETE"; then
        echo "Task complete" | tee -a "$LOG_DIR/decisions.log"
        break
    fi
    
    if echo "$RESPONSE" | grep -q "RUN_TESTS"; then
        python3 secret_spec/test_runner/run_tests.py --program "python3 solution.py" --suite public | tee -a "$LOG_DIR/test_runs.log"
    fi
    
    ITERATION=$((ITERATION + 1))
done

echo "Final iteration: $ITERATION" | tee -a "$LOG_DIR/decisions.log"
```

